title: 'network: Enable WebRTC by default on full nodes'
doc:
- audience: ['Node Dev', 'Node Operator']
  description: |-
    Accept WebRTC connections on the same UDP `--port` as used for TCP/WS connections.
    Enabled by default on full nodes, can be force-enabled on validators & collators
    with `--force-enable-webrtc`, or disabled by passing an explicit `--listen-addr`
    without WebRTC addresses.
    Only supported with litep2p network backend.

    `--listen-addr` and `--public-addr` accept a `webrtc-direct` address as
    `/<host>/udp/<port>/webrtc-direct` only. The node appends its own `/certhash/...`, being
    the only party that knows the DTLS certificate it presents, and refuses to start on an
    address that carries one already. Public addresses are completed where the configuration
    is created, so that authority discovery and the parachain bootnode advertisement publish
    the same dialable address the network backend advertises.

crates:
- name: sc-cli
  bump: major
- name: sc-network
  bump: major
# `litep2p` is a public dependency of both crates and moves 0.14 -> 0.15.
- name: sc-network-types
  bump: major
- name: sc-network-bitswap
  bump: major
- name: sc-service
  bump: patch
- name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
  bump: patch
